(footprint "BTF_Card_Mezzanine_2x07_M3"
	(version 20241229)
	(generator "hand")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "BTF daughter-card interface for the v7 CH card: the 2x07 0.100 in stacking header AND the four M3 standoff holes in ONE footprint, so they cannot be misaligned relative to each other. Drop-in replacement for the plain PinHeader_2x07_P2.54mm_Vertical on J_BTF1 - identical pad geometry (pin 1 at origin, 1.7 mm pads, 1.0 mm drill, odd pins x=0 / even x=2.54, rows at 2.54 mm) and identical 1..14 numbering, so the netlist is unchanged. FIT THE HEADER as Samtec TSW-107-xx-G-D long-post; the daughter card carries the mating ESQ-107-12-G-D socket. STANDOFF HOLES are 3.2 mm NPTH for M3, at local (1.60,-11.35), (1.60,24.85), (67.05,-11.35), (67.05,24.85) - a 65.45 x 36.20 mm pattern matching BTF_Card H1-H4 exactly. Change them to plated + a GND land only if you intend the standoffs to bond the laser case to the card - see the ground-loop note below. GEOMETRY is derived from the mating constraint (BTF J1 pin N directly above CH J_BTF1 pin N), so it is independent of where either part sits: local_x = 103.80 - y_btf, local_y = x_btf - 91.90 in BTF board coordinates. Both boards are viewed from above and the daughter card is NOT flipped, so this is a proper rotation with no mirror - confirmed by the pin1->pin2 x pin1->pin13 cross product being +38.71 on both boards. DWGS.USER shows the 43.35 x 75.00 mm daughter-card outline, the 14.35 x 31.75 mm heat-spreader cutout and the laser centre, all in true position - use them to keep the CH card clear underneath. STACK-UP: TSW-107-17-G-D header (lead style -17: post 15.74 + insulator 2.54 = 18.28 mm pin tip above this board) + ESQ-107-12-G-D socket (11.05 mm body) + M3 x 25 mm standoff gives a 25.00 mm board gap at 4.33 mm insertion, inside Samtec's 3.68-6.35 mm window. Total stack 25.0 + 1.6 board + 19.94 ZIF socket = 46.54 mm, which fits inside the 50.8 mm backplane slot pitch with 4.3 mm to spare. HEIGHT LIMITS under the card: nothing over 25 mm anywhere beneath the outline, and under 5.2 mm inside the cutout where the 25 mm aluminium heat-spreader block hangs down. WARNING - the four Wakefield 657-10ABPE heatsinks on the CH card stand 25.40 mm tall and DO NOT fit under this card: keep the daughter-card outline clear of all four. COURTYARD deliberately covers only the header and the four standoff bosses, NOT the whole card, because parts are expected to live under the mezzanine. GROUND LOOP: the laser CASE already reaches CH GND through header pin 13. If the standoffs are metal and touch the spreader they form a second path; isolate them or bond at one point deliberately.")
	(tags "btf daughter card mezzanine stacking header 2x07 tsw esq m3 standoff butterfly laser")
